# Line endings, normalised on the way in. A no-op today -- nothing tracked here
# has a CRLF in it -- and a guard for the day somebody edits on Windows, which
# is not far-fetched: the player this controls runs there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- cover art -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `binary` is `-diff -merge -text` in one word, which is all three of the things
# that should never happen to a JPEG: no textual diff, no line-ending
# translation, and no attempt to merge two versions of a photograph. Git guesses
# this correctly on its own; saying it means the guess is not load-bearing.
*.jpg binary

# ---- captured libraries ----------------------------------------------------
#
# Both of these come out of `test/fake-api/capture.ts` and are committed so that
# neither the suite nor the demo ever touches a real player. **Neither is ever
# edited by hand**, which is what the attributes below are really recording.
#
# `linguist-generated` on both: GitHub then collapses them in a pull request
# rather than opening 55,000 lines of it, and leaves them out of the language
# bar -- without it this reads as a JSON project with some TypeScript in it.
#
# `-merge` on both, because a conflict in captured data has no correct
# resolution. Git leaves the local copy and marks it conflicted; the fix is to
# re-capture, never to reconcile two halves of one photograph of a library.

# `-diff` as well, and only here: a re-capture rewrites nearly every one of this
# file's 54,000 lines, since play counts and last-played dates move whenever the
# owner listens to something. `git diff` says the files differ and stops, which
# is more use than a diff no one can read.
demo/library.json -diff -merge linguist-generated

# Deliberately still diffable, unlike the demo's. It is 1,300 lines, and a
# re-capture changes what every spec in the suite runs against -- which is
# exactly the diff a reviewer should be able to open and read.
test/fake-api/library.json -merge linguist-generated
test/fake-api/player.json -merge linguist-generated
